body:
It looks wrong to set `r_has_cs_script_instance` to `true`, you are saying there is a C# instance but returning null. In the code that calls this method:

https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/ec67cbe92628bdaf979b10594359ba6f02cf8838/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharp/Core/NativeInterop/InteropUtils.cs#L20-L31

This change would make this method return null for `[Tool]` scripts instead of trying to returning an instance of the underlying native object. This prevents the invalid cast exception, but it also prevents assigning a non-`[Tool]` instance to an exported property of a `[Tool]` object.

For example, consider these C# scripts:

```csharp
[Tool]
public partial class MyNode : Node
{
    [Export] public Resource SomeResource { get; set; }
}

public partial class MyResource : Resource { }
```

If you tried to assign an instance of `MyResource.tres` to the `MyNode.SomeResource` property, it will now print the error about accessing non-`[Tool]` C# scripts from the editor and won't assign it. However, I believe this should be allowed, and should not print any errors.
